                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ab766158-239e-3d54-a4a9-e40bc789e856",
                        "entry_id": "ab30c94d-6cf8-3d77-967f-d46b94e6fbdf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To haggle or barter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff5e5689-f58c-40e7-a3a8-b6f51bd0f00a",
                                "sense_id": "ab766158-239e-3d54-a4a9-e40bc789e856",
                                "text": "To chaffer for preferment with his gold."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "841005f1-b02a-4dc3-b13d-0efe25faf245",
                                "sense_id": "ab766158-239e-3d54-a4a9-e40bc789e856",
                                "text": "Walter declined the invitation, precisely because he wanted a dinner. He was, also, conscious that he had made a very bad bargain; but how could he chaffer and dispute about things so precious as the contents of those pages which were the very outpourings of his heart?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "50a0ae6a-a9db-46b3-a856-16d41a5fc5aa",
                                "sense_id": "ab766158-239e-3d54-a4a9-e40bc789e856",
                                "text": "While he is at the front end selling calico to some wearisome old lady, sunbonneted and chaffering, a mischievous boy is very apt to be pocketing lumps of sugar for profit, or starting the faucet of a molasses barrel for fun at the other."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "037b83b2-33fe-45a7-be19-c2dec578bf8f",
                                "sense_id": "ab766158-239e-3d54-a4a9-e40bc789e856",
                                "text": "But the people looked much like Caleb’s own. They wore dirty robes, chaffered at fruit stalls, spat, scratched."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2973776b-1355-308d-a01c-0ab6545e512b",
                        "entry_id": "ab30c94d-6cf8-3d77-967f-d46b94e6fbdf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To buy."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cdae92a1-a49b-3708-9569-a93e3d5f1122",
                        "entry_id": "ab30c94d-6cf8-3d77-967f-d46b94e6fbdf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To talk much and idly; to chatter."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f9d6986-c768-41ca-bb61-a235ebb331f5",
                                "sense_id": "cdae92a1-a49b-3708-9569-a93e3d5f1122",
                                "text": "The Dartie within him made him chaffer for five minutes with young Padwick concerning the favourite for the Cambridgeshire."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
